  "rationale": "The English cue and sense are correct, and both Malay forms can express reading aloud. However, the card overstates the regional contrast: “membaca nyaring” is also used in Malaysian Malay, while Malaysian sources support “membaca dengan kuat” as a natural construction. The relation should not imply that the two forms are cleanly Indonesia-versus-Malaysia alternatives.",
  "claim_reviews": [
    {
      "subject": "English cue and sense",
      "conclusion": "“Read aloud” correctly means reading so that others can hear.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://www.kemendikdasmen.go.id/siaran-pers/15369-lokakarya-membaca-nyaring-upaya-kemendikdasmen-bangun-kebiasaan-literasi-sejak-dini"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Indonesian answer: membaca nyaring",
      "conclusion": "Correct and established Indonesian wording for reading aloud.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://badanbahasa.kemendikdasmen.go.id/artikel-detail/3463/keajaiban-membacakan-nyaring",
        "https://bpmpjkt.kemendikdasmen.go.id/membangun-budaya-literasi-dengan-membaca-nyaring/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Malaysian answer: membaca kuat",
      "conclusion": "Understandable and attested, but “membaca dengan kuat” is a more explicitly supported Malaysian construction; the bare form should not be presented as the uniquely common Malaysian counterpart.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://prpm.dbp.gov.my/Cari1?d=175768&keyword=for+ali",
        "https://www.mcgill.ca/linguistics/files/linguistics/malay_screening_test.pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "Final relation: different-common-word",
      "conclusion": "Too strong as a regional classification. “Membaca nyaring” is also used in Malaysian Malay, so the forms are better treated as overlapping alternatives with regional or register preferences.",
      "material_risk": true,
      "evidence_refs": [
        "https://sites.google.com/moe-dl.edu.my/pb2bmmb3293-pentaksiran-dalam-pendidikan-bahasa-melayu/kemahiran-membaca/jenis-kemahiran-dan-aktiviti",
        "https://www.msocialsciences.com/index.php/mjssh/article/download/2726/2105"
      ]
    },
    {
      "subject": "False-friend contrast",
      "conclusion": "No false-friend contrast is present. The issue is overlap and regional/register variation, not divergent meaning.",
      "material_risk": false,
      "evidence_limitation": "The reviewed sources establish attestation and meaning but do not provide a controlled frequency comparison between the variants."
